{"id":"2d25e8ce649f1baf","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-thm-kato-uniqueness.md","title":"Kato Uniqueness","display":"thm-kato-uniqueness — Kato Uniqueness","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-kato-uniqueness","aliases":["58-thm-kato-uniqueness"],"display":"thm-kato-uniqueness — Kato Uniqueness","depends_on":["[[../batch20/58-df-deficiency-indices.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-kato-uniqueness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-kato-uniqueness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-kato-uniqueness — Kato Uniqueness"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"056f7b0dff6c7aee\" href=\"?note=056f7b0dff6c7aee\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-deficiency-indices.md\">../batch20/58-df-deficiency-indices.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span> (complex Hilbert space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S:D\\subseteq H\\to H\">\\(S:D\\subseteq H\\to H\\)</span> (densely defined symmetric operator)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DeficiencyIndices}_S(n_+,n_-;S,S^*,D,D^*,H)\">\\(\\mathrm{DeficiencyIndices}_S(n_+,n_-;S,S^*,D,D^*,H)\\)</span> (deficiency-index predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{UnboundedAdjoint}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{UnboundedAdjoint}_S\\)</span> (unbounded-adjoint predicate from the same dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)\">\\(\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}kato\\text{-}unbounded\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)\\leftrightarrow{}\\\\\n&amp;\\quad D\\subseteq D_A\\subseteq H\\land\\mathrm{Function}(S,D,H)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(A,D_A,H)\\land\\forall x\\in D\\;(A(x)=S(x))\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{UnboundedAdjoint}_S(A,D_A;A,D_A,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}kato\\text{-}unbounded\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)\\leftrightarrow{}\\\\\n&amp;\\quad D\\subseteq D_A\\subseteq H\\land\\mathrm{Function}(S,D,H)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(A,D_A,H)\\land\\forall x\\in D\\;(A(x)=S(x))\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{UnboundedAdjoint}_S(A,D_A;A,D_A,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kato\\text{-}uniqueness}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\n\\overline D=H\\land\\mathrm{DeficiencyIndices}_S(n_+,n_-;S,S^*,D,D^*,H)\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\left[\nn_+=n_-=0\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists!q\\in V\\;\\exists A,D_A\\in V\\;\\bigl(\nq=\\langle A,D_A\\rangle\\land\n\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)\n\\bigr)\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kato\\text{-}uniqueness}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\n\\overline D=H\\land\\mathrm{DeficiencyIndices}_S(n_+,n_-;S,S^*,D,D^*,H)\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\left[\nn_+=n_-=0\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists!q\\in V\\;\\exists A,D_A\\in V\\;\\bigl(\nq=\\langle A,D_A\\rangle\\land\n\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)\n\\bigr)\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Equality <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n_+(S)=n_-(S)\">\\(n_+(S)=n_-(S)\\)</span> alone gives existence of self-adjoint extensions; uniqueness requires both indices to vanish.</li>\n<li>Dense definition and symmetry are essential hypotheses for the deficiency-index criterion.</li>\n<li>The theorem now uses the unbounded adjoint and its domain from the deficiency-index atom.  The removed upstream extension predicate was explicitly restricted to bounded self-adjoint operators and therefore made the original unbounded statement false.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch20/58-df-deficiency-indices.md","status":"resolved","id":"056f7b0dff6c7aee","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-deficiency-indices.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"H","display":false},{"tex":"S:D\\subseteq H\\to H","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DeficiencyIndices}_S(n_+,n_-;S,S^*,D,D^*,H)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{UnboundedAdjoint}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}kato\\text{-}unbounded\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)\\leftrightarrow{}\\\\\n&\\quad D\\subseteq D_A\\subseteq H\\land\\mathrm{Function}(S,D,H)\\land\n\\mathrm{Function}(A,D_A,H)\\land\\forall x\\in D\\;(A(x)=S(x))\\\\\n&\\quad\\land\\mathrm{UnboundedAdjoint}_S(A,D_A;A,D_A,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kato\\text{-}uniqueness}\\vdash\n\\Bigl(\n\\overline D=H\\land\\mathrm{DeficiencyIndices}_S(n_+,n_-;S,S^*,D,D^*,H)\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\left[\nn_+=n_-=0\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists!q\\in V\\;\\exists A,D_A\\in V\\;\\bigl(\nq=\\langle A,D_A\\rangle\\land\n\\mathrm{UnboundedSelfAdjointExtension}_S(A,D_A;S,D,H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_H)\n\\bigr)\n\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"n_+(S)=n_-(S)","display":false}],"bytes":2006,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4248","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-thm-kato-uniqueness.md|58-thm-kato-uniqueness]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["056f7b0dff6c7aee","36d7463d215be751"]}